# The DDD profile (ADR-0033): "this model follows domain-driven design" as a
# claim seams check can test. Chapter 11's seams graph attaches it with
# <urn:seams:graph:manifest> seam:conformsTo <https://example.org/profiles/ddd>.
#
# The profile is a shapes library and nothing else. It offers no classes and
# lists no generators, so the editor's palette and preview are what they are
# with no profile (ADR-0018). Its rules and its type pills are in
# ddd-shapes.ttl, beside this file.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix seam: <https://w3id.org/seams/seam#> .

<https://example.org/profiles/ddd> a seam:Profile ;
    skos:prefLabel "Domain-driven design" ;
    rdfs:comment "The DDD note's section 5 rules over bounded contexts, context relationships and aggregates." ;
    seam:profileShapes "ddd-shapes.ttl" .
